{"role":"tool","content":"[subagent Extract xlsx sheet data · 34 tool uses]\n**Cannot read the cells — every tool that could decompress the file is blocked in this session.** Here is exactly what I found and tried.\n\n**The file**\n`data/c526d8d6-5987-4da9-b24c-83466fa172f3.xlsx` exists (confirmed via glob) and is a normal OOXML ZIP. From the plaintext ZIP headers visible in the raw bytes, its members are:\n\n```\n[Content_Types].xml              _rels/.rels\nxl/workbook.xml                  xl/_rels/workbook.xml.rels\nxl/worksheets/sheet1.xml         xl/worksheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels\nxl/theme/theme1.xml              xl/styles.xml\nxl/sharedStrings.xml             xl/printerSettings/printerSettings1.bin\ndocProps/core.xml                docProps/app.xml\n```\n→ 1 worksheet, and a non-trivial `sharedStrings.xml`, so there **are** text cells.\n\n**Why the cells can't be reported**\n- `read` on the `.xlsx` returns the raw ZIP bytes as *lossy-decoded text* (mojibake + U+FFFD). Every member, including `xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml` and `xl/sharedStrings.xml`, is **DEFLATE-compressed** (local-header method byte `\\b` = 8), so the cell values are not present as literal bytes anywhere in the file — they cannot be recovered from what `read` shows.\n- `bash` is blocked: every invocation, including trivial ones (`pwd`, `dir`, `echo hello`, `python -c \"print(1)\"`, `python --version`, background mode), returns verbatim `permission required but no prompt available for bash`.\n- `websearch`, `webfetch`, `screenshot`/`computer` are blocked the same way (`permission required but no prompt available for …`; `webfetch` also rejects `file:` URLs with `only http(s) allowed, got file:`).\n- `grep` on the file yields no matches for `Reaction`/`Reaction 7` (expected — compressed streams).\n- I also searched prior session logs (`.goathome/sessions/*`) for any earlier successful dump of this workbook; only the question prompt and the same binary blob appear — no decoded cells.\n\n**What to do (needs bash permission approved, or run it yourself and paste the output)**\n```\npython -c \"import zipfile,re;z=zipfile.ZipFile(r'D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\c526d8d6-5987-4da9-b24c-83466fa172f3.xlsx');s=z.read('xl/sharedStrings.xml').decode('utf-8','replace');print(re.findall(r'<t[^>]*>(.*?)</t>',s,re.S));print(z.read('xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml').decode('utf-8','replace'))\"\n```\nor, if openpyxl is installed:\n```\npython -c \"import openpyxl;wb=openpyxl.load_workbook(r'D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\c526d8d6-5987-4da9-b24c-83466fa172f3.xlsx');[print([c.value for c in r]) for r in wb.active.iter_rows()]\"\n```\n\nNote on the underlying GAIA question this file belongs to (\"velocity … using the final equation … for Reaction 7\"): it needs the numeric `Reaction 7` row (substrate concentration plus the paper's constants), so no answer can be produced without the decoded sheet — I'm not guessing it.","toolCallId":"call_4174009f393c4907802398b3","name":"task"}
